# OLT Gateway — variables de entorno (ejemplo prod)

```bash
export OLT_GATEWAY_ENABLED=true
export OLT_GATEWAY_MOCK=false
export OLT_GATEWAY_API_KEY=change-me
export OLT_GATEWAY_HOST=10.11.104.2
export OLT_GATEWAY_PORT=22
export OLT_GATEWAY_USER=olt-admin
export OLT_GATEWAY_PASSWORD=change-me
export OLT_GATEWAY_OLT_ID=gigafiber-ma5608t
export OLT_GATEWAY_WRITES_ENABLED=false
export OLT_GATEWAY_SYNC_INVENTORY_ENABLED=true
export OLT_GATEWAY_SYNC_INVENTORY_INTERVAL_MS=600000
export OLT_GATEWAY_SYNC_INVENTORY_INITIAL_DELAY_MS=30000
export OLT_GATEWAY_SYNC_SIGNAL_ENABLED=true
export OLT_GATEWAY_SYNC_SIGNAL_INTERVAL_MS=600000
export OLT_GATEWAY_SYNC_SIGNAL_INITIAL_DELAY_MS=90000
export OLT_GATEWAY_SYNC_SKIP_WHEN_WRITE_RUNNING=true

# WispAdmin como cliente HTTP del gateway (sin inyección in-process)
export OLT_SERVICE_PROVIDER=gateway
export OLT_SERVICE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/ispadmin/api/olt-gateway/
export OLT_SERVICE_API_KEY=change-me
```

Requiere ruta de red a la OLT (LAN o VPN). Sin ruta, usar `OLT_GATEWAY_MOCK=true`.

Writes CLI solo con `OLT_GATEWAY_WRITES_ENABLED=true` tras validación en lab.

Documentación: `.agent-docs/olt-gateway-3layer.md` y `.agent-docs/olt-gateway-read-mvp.md`
